1. Literal Listener (L0):
   d. The cat was easy to lift up.

2. Informative Speaker (S1):
   d. The cat was easy to lift up. (This is the most literal interpretation of the situation described in the story.)

3. Pragmatic Listener (L1):
   d. The cat was easy to lift up. (Given that the speaker is informative, they would choose the most appropriate utterance for the situation, which is the same as the literal interpretation in this case.)

Final Answer: d. The cat was easy to lift up.

